│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ greedy_lookahead_seed                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Improve the initial constructive solution with a bounded one-segment lookahead.           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The previous greedy initializer selected the strategy with the smallest immediate segment │
│                          │ cost. This strongly favors `direct + no post alter`, because useful block placements      │
│                          │ usually cost one extra turn now but can substantially reduce the route to the following   │
│                          │ target through a slide stopper.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The replacement first collects all strategies within one turn of the immediate optimum.   │
│                          │ For a bounded random subset of these candidates, it simulates the resulting board and     │
│                          │ evaluates the best no-post-action base strategy for the next segment. It then chooses the │
│                          │ candidate minimizing current cost plus next-segment cost. This retains cheap construction │
│                          │ time while producing much more strategically useful initial block layouts for the         │
│                          │ subsequent simulated annealing phase.                                                     │
