│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ slide_post_actions                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Extend the post-target modification neighborhood with slide-based repositioning.          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current post-action choices only allow staying at the target, toggling an adjacent    │
│                          │ block, or moving one cell and toggling a block. Since slides are the key low-cost         │
│                          │ transport mechanic, this misses useful states where the player visits a target, slides to │
│                          │ a distant stopping point in one action, and prepares a block for the following segment.   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit adds:                                                                           │
│                          │ - `Slide` only after reaching a target.                                                   │
│                          │ - `Slide + Alter` after reaching a target.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The latter uses the same three non-reverse alter directions as the existing `Move +       │
│                          │ Alter` choices. This keeps the strategy representation compact while enabling             │
│                          │ substantially more useful inter-segment positions and block layouts.                      │
