│ patch_description        │ Replace the least distinctive move-plus-alter layout: altering the square directly ahead  │
│                          │ after moving away from a target. The new layout permits moving to an adjacent square and  │
│                          │ then altering back onto the just-visited target square.                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Previously visited targets are particularly useful block locations because they are       │
│                          │ distributed throughout the board and can become slide stoppers for later targets. This    │
│                          │ also preserves the existing 12-option strategy-space size and therefore avoids reducing   │
│                          │ SA iteration throughput. The action remains legal because the player first moves off the  │
│                          │ target before altering it.                                                                │
