│ patch_description        │ This replaces the segment-strategy simulated annealing approach with a beam-search        │
│                          │ planner over complete rink states. Each beam state stores the current position,           │
│                          │ persistent block layout, action sequence, and accumulated turn count. For every required  │
│                          │ target, the planner generates several fundamentally different transition types: direct    │
│                          │ shortest movement/slide routing, unblocking a blocked target, post-target local block     │
│                          │ construction, and explicit stopper construction followed by a slide into the target. A    │
│                          │ beam preserves multiple competing block-layout designs instead of committing to one       │
│                          │ greedy local strategy or mutating a fixed strategy vector.                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The shortest path search operates directly on Move and Slide actions. The beam is scored  │
│                          │ using accumulated turns plus a lightweight look-ahead estimate toward the next target,    │
│                          │ allowing slightly more expensive block setups to survive if they improve the following    │
│                          │ transition.                                                                               │
