│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ greedy_lookahead_tiebreak                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The greedy construction currently resolves equal-cost segment strategies solely by        │
│                          │ enumeration order. Equal immediate costs can leave different block layouts and player     │
│                          │ positions, with substantially different costs for the next target.                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Keep the same immediate greedy objective, but collect all strategies tied for the minimum │
│                          │ current-segment cost. For every tied option (except on the last segment), simulate it and │
│                          │ measure the cheapest possible strategy for the following segment. Select the tied option  │
│                          │ with the lowest one-step lookahead cost. This never worsens the current greedy segment    │
│                          │ cost and gives the subsequent SA search a more promising feasible initial state, while    │
│                          │ only adding work when strategies actually tie.                                            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
