╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ neutral_state_exploration                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The greedy single-segment neighborhood currently keeps only a strictly cheaper strategy   │
│                          │ for the current segment. This discards strategies with the same immediate turn cost even  │
│                          │ when they leave a different player position or block layout, both of which can            │
│                          │ substantially improve subsequent segments.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Use reservoir sampling among equal-cost strategies in the sampled subset. The complete    │
│                          │ suffix is still evaluated afterwards, so a neutral local replacement is accepted only     │
│                          │ when its downstream effect is beneficial (or under the existing simulated-annealing       │
│                          │ rule). This increases exploration of useful block configurations without admitting        │
│                          │ locally worse candidates in this operator.                                                │
